[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-SEL-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Complete selection preflight
STATEMENT: All applicable selection predicates shall be evaluated before any test body is invoked. A later malformed or timed-out regex shall not leave earlier test-body side effects.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-033
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/SharpTestBench/RegressionSelection.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/SharpTestBench/Regression.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tests/SelectionPlanning60.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tests/SelectionPlanning62rest.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-SEL-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stable complete-order case seeds
STATEMENT: Seeds shall be allocated in complete stage and ordinal-qualified-name order before filtering. Case variants shall retain declaration order. Seed addition shall wrap modulo 2^64 and selected cases shall keep their full-discovery seeds.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-033
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/SharpTestBench/RegressionSelection.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tests/SelectionPlanning60.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-SEL-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Explicit testcase skip override
STATEMENT: Testcase mode shall bypass only an explicit SimTest.Skip declaration. Backend exclusion, stopped-stage policy, expected-exception rules, cancellation, cleanup and leak guards shall remain effective. Discovery shall retain declared skip metadata.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-033
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/SharpTestBench/Regression.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tests/SelectionPlanning60.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-SEL-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Unambiguous planned identities
STATEMENT: Duplicate qualified case identities shall be rejected during complete planning before any test body executes.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-033
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/SharpTestBench/RegressionSelection.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tests/SelectionPlanning60.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tests/SelectionPlanning62rest.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-EXP-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded public-export review
STATEMENT: Public-export decisions shall bind their reviewed module and explicit export name to source hashes, the upstream pin and implementation or gap evidence. Reviewed export counts shall not be reported as parity percentages or full dynamic-surface completeness.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-001
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tools/SharpTestBench.Tools/ExportAuditCommand.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tools.Tests/SelectionTools66.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-EXP-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Export evidence rejection
STATEMENT: Export validation shall reject stale hashes, unknown or duplicate reviewed exports, malformed metadata, missing anchors and evidence paths outside the repository.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-001
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tools/SharpTestBench.Tools/ExportAuditCommand.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tools.Tests/SelectionTools66.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-PRO-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: CRC stream behavior
STATEMENT: The local CRC stream fixture shall preserve accepted packet order and check its defined polynomial, packet-boundary state, backpressure, length and reset behavior against independent packet history.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-PRO-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Round-robin arbitration behavior
STATEMENT: The local four-request arbiter fixture shall check enabled grants, acknowledged rotation, pointer hold, request withdrawal and reset against independent request and fairness expectations.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-PRO-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Byte-enabled register-bank behavior
STATEMENT: The local eight-word register bank shall check read enable, byte lanes, write qualification, read-before-write collisions and reset against an independent byte store.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-PRO-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Oracle sensitivity and recovery
STATEMENT: Protocol negative controls shall demonstrate that a deliberate native-output fault is detected before transaction consumption and that reset or cancellation recovery retains the defined accounting invariants.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-VER-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Scoped managed coverage
STATEMENT: Verification shall collect line and branch coverage for all four production assemblies, identify generated-source contributions and document unmeasured native, HDL and CLI execution scope. Coverage shall not be treated as proof of correctness.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-041

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-VER-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Adversarial and property verification
STATEMENT: Relevant interfaces shall be checked with malformed inputs, negative tests, deliberate code mutations, seeded fuzzing and randomized property checks. Evidence shall retain replay seeds, counterexamples, mutation outcomes and limitations, distinguishing compile failures from killed mutants.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-041
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SelectionQuality/Properties.fsx
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SelectionQuality/Mutations.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SelectionQuality/PlannerMutations.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-VER-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Preserved runner attestation
STATEMENT: Paired-runner qualification shall independently check expected qualified identities, effective seeds, statuses and bound inputs. Required manifests shall continue rejecting skipped cases, and existing result, discovery, coverage and run-evidence schemas shall remain unchanged.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-041
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tools/SharpTestBench.Tools/SelectionScenarioEvidence.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tools.Tests/SelectionTools70.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STB-VER-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Discovered core-managed test inventory
STATEMENT: The managed-tests CLI shall discover the current core-suite case inventory, require complete passing baseline evidence, and demonstrate exactly one named failing assertion in an isolated assembly without treating build failures or missing cases as success.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STB-041
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tools/SharpTestBench.Tools/ManagedTestsCommand.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/SharpTestBench.Tools.Tests/SelectionToolsManagedValidation.cs
